## Acerca de COOPI

COOPI Cooperazione Internazionale es una ONG laica e independiente, fundada en Milán en 1965. Lleva a cabo proyectos de desarrollo para contribuir a la lucha contra las desigualdades y programas de emergencia para apoyar a las personas afectadas por desastres naturales o conflictos. Actualmente, COOPI está presente en 33 países de África, Oriente Medio, América Latina y Caribe.

Desde 2019 COOPI establece una presencia en Venezuela, y a partir de julio de 2020, inicia un programa regional que se implementa en asociación con organizaciones venezolanas y en coordinación con instituciones locales e internacionales, en el marco de los planes de respuesta vigentes. En los últimos años COOPI ha ampliado sus intervenciones y actualmente ejecuta proyectos con diferentes donantes en Caracas, Sucre, Delta Amacuro y Bolivar, en protección (GBV, trata y tráfico de personas), salud sexual reproductiva, WASH (agua, saneamiento e higiene), alimentación escolar y fortalecimiento institucional.

En coincidencia con el lanzamiento de un nuevo proyecto multisectorial con diferentes socios internacionales y nacionales, COOPI requiere de la contratación de un Logista Pais / Gerente de Logística.

## Objetivo/descripción del puesto

El Logista País será responsable de la supervisión, planificación y coordinación de las actividades logísticas dentro de los proyectos de COOPI, asegurando que se cumplan los estándares y procedimientos establecidos en la organización, así como las normas nacionales e internacionales aplicables.

El objetivo principal del Logista País es garantizar la correcta gestión y ejecución de las operaciones logísticas necesarias para el desarrollo de proyectos de la Organización, asegurando la adecuada distribución de recursos, el manejo eficiente de suministros y equipos, y el cumplimiento de las normativas de seguridad y calidad. Este rol incluye la coordinación de la cadena de suministro, el transporte y la gestión de inventarios.

## Áreas de responsabilidad

**Planificación y control**

- Planificar y coordinar todas las actividades logísticas dentro de los proyectos de la ONG, incluyendo el transporte, almacenamiento y distribución de bienes y equipos;
- Gestionar la cadena de suministro y coordinar con proveedores y otros actores clave para asegurar la entrega oportuna de los suministros necesarios;
- Garantizar la aplicación de los procedimientos internos de la ONG y de las políticas de control de calidad en todas las actividades logísticas, así como en el manejo de inventarios;
- Garantizar el cumplimiento de los estándares de calidad y transparencia de acuerdo a los requerimientos de la organización y de los donantes;
- Asegurar que las actividades logísticas se alineen con las normativas nacionales e internacionales de seguridad, sostenibilidad y protección ambiental;
- Apoyar a los Coordinadores de Proyecto en la elaboración de los planes de compras según los presupuestos asignados por proyecto, realizando seguimiento periódico de la planificación y desarrollo del mismo en aspecto logísticos;
- Asegurar la actualización de forma periódica de la base de datos de proveedores, incluyendo evaluaciones, análisis técnicos y de mercado según objeto social de los proveedores y desempeño;
- Apoyar en la preparación de propuesta de financiación y en la presentación de los informes provisionales y finales de los proyectos asignados.

**Gestión logística y soporte**

- Supervisar la gestión de todos los aspectos logísticos relacionados con las operaciones de la misión y con los programas/proyectos asignados, bajo la supervisión de la Coordinación País;
- Gestionar las diferentes fases de los procesos de compra (aprobación, solicitud y análisis de cotizaciones, pedidos, contratos, órdenes de compra, gestión de pagos), de acuerdo a los procedimientos establecidos para cada categoría de bienes y servicios;
- Asegurar la correcta implementación de los movimientos de la organización a nivel coordinación y bases;
- Asegurar el correcto funcionamiento de los equipo informáticos de la organización, a través de asistencia directa y servicios externos;
- Asegurar la gestión y mantenimiento de los espacios de oficina de la organización y de la flota de vehículos;
- Supervisar la recepción, almacenamiento y ensamblaje, cuando requerido, de insumos y materiales, así como su traslado a los lugares de entrega;
- Supervisar, en coordinación con el equipo administrativo, el registro y archivo de los documentos referentes a la adquisición, garantía, depreciación y mantenimiento de equipos y bienes durables en el marco de los proyectos, así como su transferencia de un proyecto a otro y/o a los beneficiarios directos y/o a contrapartes locales;
- Gestionar el correcto mantenimiento de los activos propiedad de COOPI o adquiridos por los proyectos, utilizando las herramientas corporativas;
- Apoyar a la Coordinación País en la actualización periódica y aplicación del plan de seguridad, velando para que las medidas previstas sean respetadas de manera adecuada;
- Realizar evaluaciones de los bienes de la organización para garantizar que se cumplan las condiciones mínimas de seguridad, manteniendo una política de prevención de pérdidas y los daños de los bienes de la organización;
- Llevar a cabo aquellas tareas inherentes a los objetivos del puesto, que sean solicitadas por el equipo de Coordinación País según contexto y necesidades de los proyectos que ejecuta la organización.

**Coordinacion y representación**

- Coordinar, formar y evaluar el personal logístico bajo su supervisión directa;
- Formar al equipo logístico de las bases y supervisar el desempeño de las tareas de gestión logística;
- Formar y proporcionar asistencia técnica a los equipos de los socios locales en la implementación de las políticas y procesos logísticos de los proyectos en ejecución;
- Participar en las reuniones de coordinación internas liderando sesiones de trabajo según requerido;
- Representar a la organización en las reuniones de coordinación externa (cluster, grupos de trabajo, consorcios).

## Perfil deseado

**ESENCIALES**

- Estudios profesionales (licenciatura, deseable postgrado o master) en Logística, Comercio, Cadenas de Aprovisionamiento, Ingeniería, Ciencias Económicas, Administración de Empresas y/o afines;
- Experiencia de mínimo 5 en gestión logística, preferiblemente en el sector humanitario o en ONGs.;
- Experiencia demostrable en gestión de compras y de inventarios, así como conocimiento de los principales sistemas y programas de gestión;
- Experiencia en la gestión de equipo informático y IT;
- Experiencia en el trato directo con proveedores y con contrapartes comerciales;
- Capacidad de trabajar de forma autónoma y bajo presión, en contextos con elevadas complejidades;
- Excelente capacidad de trabajo en equipo, en ambientes multiculturales y con equipos multidisciplinares;
- Honestidad, actitud proactiva y resolutiva, sentido común, capacidad analítica y discreción;
- Flexibilidad y disponibilidad a viajar en el interior del país;
- Respeto de la carta de valores de la organización y de los principios humanitarios;
- Idioma castellano;
- Manejo de herramientas informáticas y ofimáticas;

**DESEABLES**
- Experiencia en el ámbito de la ayuda humanitaria y/o cooperación al desarrollo;
- Experiencia en la gestión logística de proyectos de emergencia;
- Experiencia en sistematización de procesos y elaboración de documentos e informes;
- Experiencia en la supervisión o acompañamiento a socios locales y contrapartes;
- Idioma inglés altamente valorado;
- Capacidad para trabajar bajo presión;
- Capacidad para organizar el trabajo de forma independiente y priorizar tareas;
- Nacionalidad: venezolana o permiso para trabajar en el país;
- Licencia de conducir Vigente

**Position: GIS Officer-Sudan**
**Duty Station: Nairobi**
**Starting Date: January 2027**
**Type of Contract: Fixed Term**
**Duration: 6 Months**

REACH is a joint initiative of two INGOs ([IMPACT Initiatives](http://www.impact-initiatives.org/) and [ACTED](http://www.acted.org/)). REACH purpose is to promote efficient, inclusive and integrated local planning, aid response and service delivery in areas affected by crisis\*.\* AGORA is a localized approach for assessing needs, planning response and coordinating interventions in crisis affected territories. AGORA approach aims at 1) developing multi-stakeholder-are-based recovery stabilization plans; 2) promoting citizens and civil society engagement; 3) provide technical assistance to local institutional actors; 3) support the implementation of settlement recovery and stabilization plans.

**COUNTRY PROFILE**

Clashes between the Sudanese Armed Forces (SAF) and the Rapid Support Forces (RSF) erupted in Khartoum on 15 April 2023 and spread quickly across the country. Civilians have fled areas affected by fighting in large numbers, including to Chad, Egypt and South Sudan. Prices of food, fuel and other basic goods have skyrocketed skyrocketing, making critical goods unaffordable for many people. Half of Sudan’s population are in need of humanitarian assistance, and the country is on the verge of a catastrophic hunger crisis. Humanitarian organizations are racing to respond to the most pressing needs wherever and whenever feasible, with access issues complicating the ability of actors to respond. In this fast-evolving context, IMPACT Initiatives is working to inform the emergency response to enable effective prioritization with scarce resources.

## **Assignment**

Under the line management of the GIS manager and the supervision of the Research Manager, the GIS Officer will be responsible for the design of data processes (including GIS data), the management of large sets of data, and primarily supporting of the team with data-related tasks, including cleaning, analysis, reporting, and automating recurring tasks. He/she will also be asked to support on designing data collection tools that include a GIS component, ensuring (spatial) data quality, geo-spatial analysis, drafting of maps, and (as relevant) production of web maps and information management systems. Detailed requirements below.

He/she will also be asked to provide technical inputs in all stages of the research cycle. He/she ensures an efficient and transparent use of resources required for project implementation.

## **Functions**

**GIS ACTIVITIES**

**1. Preparation, conception and production of maps**

- Identify map information needs.
- Identify and access map information sources.
- Ensure accurate linkages between spatial databases and assessment data,
- Ensures that the produced maps meet the requirements of REACH and concerned partners.

**2. Supervision and monitoring of mapping related data collection**

- Conceptualize methodologies for collecting data in the field, as according to need;
- Organize and supervise GIS field missions;
- Monitor accuracy of data collected.
- Cross check data collected in the field, ensure regular updates and solve eventual discrepancies;

**3. GIS product conceptualizing**

- Implementation GIS components in approved projects and developing map templates;
- Contribute to the strategic and programmatic development of the country team

**4. GIS capacity training**

- Develop internal training for assessment, and where relevant ACTED staff on data management, GIS and mapping

**DATABASE/DATA MANAGEMENT ACTIVITIES**

The REACH GIS Officer will manage the maintenance of database(s) for the consolidation of all assessment-related and GIS data in country. He/she will ensure the capitalization of tools and procedures related to mapping and databases. Furthermore, he/she will support the assessment team in the collection and management of spatial datasets, verification and update of the collected data. He/she will monitor the accuracy of collected data.

**TECHNICAL SUPPORT**

The REACH GIS Specialist will contribute towards the identification and implementation of effective and adapted technical solutions and partnerships. The REACH GIS Specialist will provide technical backstopping of database to GIS/DB team and provide capacity-building to GIS/DB team related to database maintenance and advanced GIS techniques. He/she will also support the collection of spatial datasets and integration with REACH activities. The GIS/Data specialist will also contribute to drafting and implementation of a high-level GIS and Data management strategy.

**RESEARCH DESIGN**

In collaboration with the in-country assessment team, and under the supervision of the GIS Specialist, the Data/GIS Specialist will be responsible for providing support to the design of AGORA. This includes:

- Mapping and analysing secondary data in coordination with the assessment officer(s);
- Contributing to the drafting of the assessment ToRs with a specific focus on the analysis plan, and related mapping, as well as data management plan;
- Supporting the development of qualitative and quantitative data collection tools, ensuring GIS requirements of the assessment are met;
- In coordination with relevant assessment officer(s), support construction of quantitative sample and qualitative checks.

**RESEARCH IMPLEMENTATION**

Under the supervision of the Senior GIS Officer, in collaboration with the assessment and field teams, the Data/GIS Officer will be asked, to support the implementation of data collection, regarding:

- Tool design and testing;
- Training of enumerators for primary data collection and technical support during data collection if needed;
- Oversight of data collection, in line with agreed TORs, including data quality checks, cleaning, spatial verification and validation as part of daily assessment checks;
- Ensure that collected data is properly geo-referenced, enabling the production of maps and related products.

**EXTERNAL ENGAGEMENT**

- Promote active use of datasets and research findings by partners and the broader humanitarian community for their decision making.
- After validation by line manager, present research findings to relevant third parties in order to enhance their use and impact;
- Ensure that all partner engagement and all external relations are clearly documented and communicated with the line manager and relevant colleagues.
- More generally, contribute to the creation of a positive image and overall credibility of the organization, notably through the application of IMPACT’s mandate, ethics, values and standpoint with regard to other actors.

**OUTPUT PRODUCTION**

In collaboration with the in-country assessment team and the Report unit at IMPACT HQ (Geneva), the Data/GIS specialist will be responsible for producing and/or overseeing the production of Data/GIS products (datasets, dashboards, maps), which comply with IMPACT’s guidelines. This includes:

- Ensure that all Data/GIS products are validated by IMPACT HQ before external release;
- When relevant, in close coordination with IMPACT HQ, support the regular maintenance and update of web GIS products;
- Liaise with IMPACT HQ on the procurement of UNOSAT services and satellite imagery.

**DATA CONFIDENTIALITY AND PROTECTION**

The GIS Specialist will maintain the strictest confidentiality on all data collected and related processes, ensuring full compliance with IMPACT’s data protection policy and SOPs. He/she will actively take measures to prevent the unauthorized sharing of any information and data belonging to IMPACT and its partners, or collected during his/her assignment with IMPACT.

## **EXPERIENCE AND QUALIFICATION**

- Master degree in a relevant discipline (Geography, Geomatics, Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Information Management Systems, Statistics, Mathematics, etc.). Or, Bachelor’s degree in GIS or related discipline with additional relevant work experience;
- 1 year of experience in GIS/Database/Remote sensing, preferably in humanitarian context;
- Excellent analytical skills;
- Proficient knowledge of QGIS/ArcGIS;
- Experience with cleaning and analysing large datasets required;
- Strong skills in Excel required;
- Good understanding of various sampling frameworks;
- Experience with or willingness to learn on R software;
- Ability to operate in a cross-cultural environment requiring flexibility;
- Ability to work independently;
- Written and spoken fluency in English required;
- Experience with or willingness to learn: ArcGIS Online environment, FME, Google Earth Engine, OpenStreet Map, R, and/or Tableau;
- Experience with or willingness to learn: Kobo, ODK or similar mobile data collection tools.

**About Us**

The Platform for Peace and Humanity was established with the belief that a more peaceful world is possible. Founded in Slovakia in 2016, the Platform draws on Czechoslovakia’s historical experiences with totalitarian regimes, occupation and conflict, as well as its peaceful transition into the Czech Republic and Slovakia. Being aware of the necessity of standing against violations of international law, including illegal acts of aggression, the Platform’s first initiative was to advocate for a stronger international response to the crime of aggression by the International Criminal Court. Slovakia and the Czech Republic stand out globally for enshrining an unconditional model of universal jurisdiction, allowing for the prosecution of individuals for serious international crimes—such as genocide, war crimes, and crimes against humanity—regardless of where the crime occurred or the nationality of the perpetrator or victim. The Platform has actively supported this principle, submitting cases to investigators and representing victims based on universal jurisdiction, such as for crimes against humanity and war crimes committed in Ukraine.

**Our Purpose**

The Platform for Peace and Humanity exists to promote, advance, and achieve sustainable international peace through the mutual effort, passion, and commitment of like-minded individuals dedicated to our shared humanity.

**Our Goals**

- To deliver justice for victims and survivors of conflict-related violence and other human rights violations.
- To support institutions, organisations, and individuals that work toward sustainable peace and social justice.

**Our approach**

- We investigate abuses and invoke international and domestic accountability mechanisms through legal assistance, litigation, advocacy, and documenting violations of international law and human rights.
- We engage in monitoring, research, and analysis of the humanitarian implications of current conflicts, violations of international law, and the structural vulnerabilities that prevent the realisation of human rights around the world.
- We collaborate with institutions, organisations, and individuals who share our commitment to promoting sustainable peace, social justice, and human rights worldwide.

**Position Overview**:

The Platform for Peace and Humanity is currently seeking a talented volunteer Graphics Designer. The volunteer will help transform complex research and data into compelling, accessible, and visually engaging publications and content for social media.

This is a voluntary, unpaid role and is ideal for early-career professionals in graphics design, with a strong interest in human rights, international peace and security and/or social justice. Applicants should take a keen interest in the vision and objectives of the Platform.

**Deadline to apply:** 9 December 2026

**Start date**: ASAP

**Duration**: minimum 12 months, including a one-month probationary period

**Location:** Home office (remote)

**Time commitment**: 10 hr/week, flexible work hours

**Duties and responsibilities:**

- Design and layout reports, briefings, fact sheets, and other publications;
- Create infographics, graphics, charts, maps, and visual assets that communicate complex information clearly;
- Ensure visual consistency across reports, presentations, social media, and advocacy materials;
- Collaborate closely with team members throughout the publication process;
- Prepare print-ready and digital files according to publication standards;
- Support the development and maintenance of organisational branding and visual identity

**Requirements:**

- Proven professional experience in graphic design, preferably for NGOs, research organisations, publishers, media outlets, or advocacy groups;
- Advanced proficiency in Adobe InDesign or alternative software and demonstrated experience designing long-form publications and reports;
- Strong skills in Adobe Creative Suite;
- Experience using Canva and other digital design platforms;
- Strong understanding of typography, layout design, and information visualisation;
- Excellent attention to detail
- Professional-level English;
- Strong communication and inter-personal skills;
- Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Sharepoint, Teams) and Google Workspace;
- Demonstrated passion and dedication to the mission and values of the Platform
- Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines

**What we offer:**

- Opportunities to gain valuable experience in an international NGO context and expand one’s professional network internationally.
- Opportunity to build one’s portfolio of graphics work, including publications crediting the graphics designer
- A profile on the Platform’s website and visibility in a global expert network.

Deputy Head of Consortium DOVIRA (Developing Organized Vital Interventions for Relief and Assistance of the most vulnerable populations in Ukraine)

**Country Programme:** Ukraine

**Base:** Kyiv, Ukraine with frequent field trips

**Line Manager:** Head of Consortium

**People in Need** (PIN) is a Czech-based international non-governmental organization (NGO) that has provided humanitarian and development assistance across more than 20 countries since 1992. Today, PIN stands as one of the largest organizations of its kind in Central and Eastern Europe, supporting vulnerable communities in Asia, Africa, the Middle East, and Eastern Europe. PIN empowers civil society, advocates for human rights, and promotes social inclusion both at home and abroad.

## **About the role:**

Deputy Head of Consortium (DHoC) provides coordination and oversight support to Head of Consortium, especially in direct follow up on implementation of the award activities, ensuring synergies and integration among partners’ work, high quality of the deliverables, alignment with clusters standards as well as with the area-based coordination priorities and gaps analysis. DHoC also is the main focal point for the cooperation with MEAL, ensuring relevant processes and systems for assessments, baseline, endline, mid-term reviews are in place and provide necessary information as well as collects learning and good practices for overall programme improvements.

## **About DOVIRA:**

DOVIRA programme aims to enhance the resilience and well-being of war-affected communities across East, West, North and South Ukraine by improving access to adequate housing, mental health and psychosocial support, safe drinking water, hygiene assistance and livelihood opportunities.

**Internal relations:**

The DHoC reports directly to Head of Consortium and coordinates closely with PIN programme (programme quality, grants and partnership management) and MEAL focal points

**External relations:**

The DHoC is the main focal point for PIN as well as Consortium and Implementing Partners key programme staff, supporting them in implementation as per the award timeline, budget, set-up objectives and quality standards. The DHoC leads the Consortium Project Management Unit, ensuring complementarity of the partners’ work, as well leads on lessons learned discussions and programme or activities adaptation based on the findings.

## **Main Duties & Responsibilities:**

**Project Cycle Management**

- Facilitates coordination, communication, collaboration and information sharing on relevant programmatic issues with Consortium and Implementing Partners
- Ensures that Consortium activities are implemented according to the initially agreed work plan and programme design as reflected in the partnership agreement;
- Coordinates and oversee data management procedures for Consortium and Implementing Partners activities;
- Conducts regular programme review meetings for PIN as well as the Consortium and Implementing partners;
- Ensures the programme progress is effectively monitored through regular data collection, analysis of indicators and activities and documented with proper verification;
- Conducts regular follow-up of Consortium and Implementing Partners work plans to identify and address any delays in a timely and effective manner;
- Monitors output achievement, cash burn rates, and ensure timely completion of the programme activities;
- Conducts periodic visits to programme location to validate progress reports, identify problems and issues to address during Consortium Project Management Unit meetings and make recommendations for improvement;
- Advise consortium Programme Managers to adapt implementation of the programme according to monitoring and evaluation findings.

**Communication and Coordination**

- Facilitates Consortium Project Management Unit and other coordination meetings with Consortium and Implementing Partners on program management issues;
- Cooperates closely with PIN and Consortium and Implementing Partners program departments on programmatic synergies and complementarities with the aim to identify issues to address and make recommendations for improvement.

**Compliance, Budget and Finance**

- In collaboration with PIN Head of Quality and Programme Development as well as respective Technical Leads, ensures that all approval requests are in-line with the assigned donor’s requirements and coordinates with PIN Grants Management focal point their submission a timely manner;
- In collaboration with focal point from Finance department, conducts regular budget and finance meetings with Consortium partners to ensure the spending is according to the initially agreed budget.

**Programme Development and Quality**

- Directly responsible for quality assurance of performance measures (e.g. outcome indicators, interim milestones, and the efficacy of the overall monitoring and evaluation systems);
- Oversees the development and implementation of the Monitoring and Evaluation framework for the Consortium and be available to provide programmatic and monitoring guidance as needed;
- Develops, in coordination with the Consortium partners, US Department of State, and other stakeholders, lessons learned in the design and implementation of Consortium activities and means of responding to these.

**Grants Management, overseen in coordination with PIN Grants Management focal point**

- Preparation of necessary reporting framework for Consortium and Implementation Partners, including relevant guidelines, templates and deadlines
- Ensuring reporting for all Consortium and Implementation Partners, according to donor and PIN requirements, is respected by all according to agreed deadlines;
- Collection and consolidation of narrative reports from consortium members for donor reporting;
- Consolidation and finalization of narrative reports, assistance with review and approval of financial reporting.
- Preparation of documentation necessary for any project modifications, including budget revisions, amendments, or extensions. Ensure such changes are made in close consultation with the consortium partners.

## **Requirements:**

- Past experience in overseeing implementation of complex, multisectoral programmes in conflict settings
- Demonstrated experience in donor compliance, budget monitoring, partner agreements and consolidated narrative and financial reporting.
- Experience in networking, partnership building and representation skills
- Strong knowledge of strategic project planning, management cycles, as well as knowledge management
- Strong organizational and documentation skills, capable of managing multiple competing deliverables
- Experience in early recovery and development and humanitarian programming, preferably in the region
- University degree in relevant field
- Familiarity with the conflicts’ settings
- Technical expertise within one of the strategic sectors will be an advantage (WASH, Shelter, Economic Recovery, Social protection and inclusion).
- Excellent communication, facilitation and negotiation skills, excellent spoken and written English
- Knowledge of Russian or Ukrainian is a preference
- Dynamic and result-oriented with ability to organize and plan effectively, responsible and systematic
- Reliable and self-reliant personality with responsible and systematic approach to work
- Critical analysis and problem-solving skills
- Ability to work in difficult conditions and under pressure
- Cultural sensitivity
- Strong ability and willingness to transfer knowledge
- Willing to travel within the country
- Reliable and self-reliant

The recruitment is contingent upon confirmation of the funding.

## **We offer:**

- Working environment in a well-established humanitarian organization in a challenging context;
- **Starting Salary** based on PIN’s salary scale and HR policies, between 2900-3300 EUR;
- **Additional allowances include**:
- Monthly Subsistence Allowance of 1440 EUR;
- Monthly Hardship Allowance of 400 EUR;
- Accommodation provided by PIN/Monthly Housing Allowance up to 1000 EUR;
- **Time off and Rest:**
- 25 days of holiday annually;
- 10 sick days
- Rest & Recreation (R&R) policy in place: 3x 5 days of leave per year with 350 Eur lump sum allowance per each leave.
- **Travel benefits:**
- Reimbursement of travel expenses with travel to the country of residence once every 6 months of work;
- Reimbursement of costs of visas and vaccinations; assistance with the visa application procedure;
- Reimbursement for the medical check-up before and after the deployment;
- Travel health insurance covering medical care, incl. the repatriation;
- **Health and Well-being:**
- 24/7 Medical Support available online;
- Free psychological consultations available online;
- **Professional Development:** Free access to e-learning platforms and PIN Learning Hub; PIN’s global Induction Training, and tailored capacity-building opportunities, including Hostile Environment Awareness Training (HEAT);

## **Security situation in Ukraine**

Humanitarian workers continue to operate throughout Ukraine, although the front-line areas are being shelled almost constantly, and main cities are being targeted with missiles and UAVs quite regularly. PIN security SOPs require PIN staff to proceed to shelter should the risk level be assessed by the Security Department as the highest (launch of missiles or drones) and remain there until the air raid siren is cancelled, which cumulatively can be several times a week, occasionally for several hours at a time (although shorter periods are as well occurring). While air strikes that were targeting energy, infrastructure have finished after winter, they have succeeded in reaching their goals and are likely to resume in late autumn/winter. At the moment military and civilian objects are being targeted, including the west of Ukraine. While Kyiv enjoys relatively strong air defence systems that are intercepting most of the missiles and UAVs, other regions are covered much less significantly which results in bigger damage. Outside of the areas in the vicinity to the contact line, services such as medical care, shops, public transportation as well as restaurants or leisure facilities remain operational.

**Line Manager:** SYR Country Director

**Contract Length:** 1 year

**Start date:** Feb 2027

## **Position Summary**

The Operations Director (OD) is a member of the country management team (CMT) together with the Country Director (CD) and Programs Director (PD). The OD shares responsibility for the effective and efficient delivery of People in Need’s (PIN) country programme. Specifically, the role of the OD is to manage and improve the support systems and operations required to achieve this objective comprising of the Finance, Human Resources, Logistics and Procurement departments. In performing this role, the OD also ensures an enabling environment for the implementation of the country programme, while maintaining operations and systems that meet with the accountability requirements of PIN and its donors.

## **Reporting Relations & Interdependencies with Other Functions**

The OD´s line manager is the Country Director (CD). Technically the OD is supervised by the Deputy Finance and Operations Director (DFOD) based at HQ.

At country programme level, the OD is the line manager of Logistics and Procurement Manager, Finance Manager and HR Manager. The OD also works closely with Programs Director, Programme Managers (ProgMs), the Head of Offices other departments mainly Liaison, Security, Accountability, MEAL department and other.

At headquarters (HQ) level, apart from the DFOD, her/his counterparts on the methodological level is the Finance Coordinator, Accounting Manager, Finance Advisory Unit, Logistics&Procurement Unit, Accounting unit, HQ HR Department, HQ Safeguarding as well as the Legal and Compliance department.

## **Duties & Responsibilities**

### **Strategic Leadership**

- As part of the Country Management Team (CMT), the OD assists the CD in the management of the country programme, participates in the senior management meetings, and pro-actively takes part in the decision-making processes;
- Ensures that systems and operations support the implementation of the country programme strategy and that logistics, procurement and financial procedures and regulations are implemented in full transparency and in accordance with donor and PIN rules;
- In areas of expertise represents PIN towards local authorities, donors, partners, and other stakeholders;
- Is responsible for adequate staffing of all supervised departments in order to achieve efficient delivery of People in Need’s (PIN) country programme;
- Promotes team spirit, a culture of respect, personal responsibility, transparency, and openness;
- OD acts as the Deputy CD in CD’s absence if assigned.

### **Quality & Risk Management**

- The OD ensures that PIN policies and guidelines related to HR, logistics & procurement and finance are known and respected;
- supervises the support departments and functions under his/her line management, and sets up effective internal coordination and communication;
- promotes participation and accountability towards local authorities, local partners, and donors;
- in cooperation with CD, prepares contingency plans, manages risks and coordinates risk mitigation measures.

### **Human Resources & Capacity Development**

- The OD is familiar with PIN HR procedures and ensures that all country programme staff follows them;
- manages the national HR team and ensures it has sufficient capacity both in number and qualification of HR personnel;
- makes sure that relevant country programme HR procedures are in place and respected, and updates them on regular basis;
- supervises the process of internal and external recruitment of national staff;
- establishes system of in-country induction for both international and national staff;
- conducts induction training to new staff in operational procedures, as well as “DOs and DON’Ts” of the country programme;
- ensures that regular staff evaluation is in place and that bonuses and capacity development tools are being used according to HR guidelines;
- ensures that the contract termination procedures are followed properly;
- in coordination with FM, ensure that all HR administration systems for country programme are operating properly, in particular overseeing the proper implementation of administrative issues related to HR;
- together with the country programme senior management (CD, PD etc.) and national HR personnel, cooperate with HQ HR department on HR audits, setting and improving of HR procedures, and supporting their implementation;
- together with the national HR personnel, inform HQ HR about current HR related needs and requests from country programmes, at minimum within Quarterly report;
- takes part in the investigation procedures related to the reporting of breach of PIN Code of Conduct or other disciplinary issues if requested;
- Ensures HR systems (HRIS, ELO, Navision) are properly set-up, administrated and used.

### **Finance Management**

- The OD makes sure that relevant country programme financial and administrative procedures are in place and respected;
- oversees the operations of the financial team in all sectors, including budgeting, reporting, and accounting of the country programme;
- ensures communication between Finance and other departments with special focus on budget management;
- ensures financial and administrative systems (ELO, Navision) are properly administrated and used by the whole country programme;
- ensures the timely completion of CP documents needed for the yearly closure procedure;
- gives guidance and support to FM/Logs Manager for finance and procurement related communication with donors.

### **Logistics & Procurement**

- The OD oversees operations of the Logistics&procurement department in all sectors (office and compound/guesthouse management, fleet, transport, communication, IT);
- oversees assets and stock management systems;
- oversees procurement system following all relevant donor and PIN guidelines and procedures, and considering relevant risks;
- Oversees the development of greening operations processes
- makes sure relevant country programme procurement guidelines are in place and are respected;
- supervises and advises the country programme Procurement Officer and makes sure country programme procurement plan is developed and regularly maintained;
- ensures that current procurement documents are up to date;
- on a regular basis, audits the procurement process in order to highlight flaws and pressures associated with operating in the country programme context;
- implements or strengthens systems of oversight and prevention of corruption;
- oversees logistics budgets, improves needs planning, and contributes to planning needs for new projects with regards to logistics;
- ensures effective and efficient operational spending and provides commentary on the operational setup to other members of country programme senior management;
- establishes and supervises tools for cost effective office and operational management in cooperation with Finance department;
- supervises and organizes yearly inventories;
- supervises programme staff for the regular update of stock table (for donation to beneficiaries) and ensures that donation contracts are systematically prepared for any final donation;

### **Liaison with public authorities**

- In general, the OD ensures that all obligations towards local authorities (annual audit, annual reports, fiscal financial reports, tax reports etc.) are respected and met in a timely manner;
- ensures that all taxes are paid in line with national regulatory framework;
- ensures that tax exemption (when possible) will be applied by NGO;
- In coordination with the CD and other relevant colleagues, ensures that all agenda related to permits, licences, and registrations are dealt with as and when required.

### **Operational support in Partnership and localisation**

- Supervising the transparency of the due diligence and partner selection process, PATs, capacity development plans of partners in the areas of finance, logistics and procurement;
- Ensure that administrative and financial processes and procedures related to partnerships and sub grants are standardized and consistently implemented throughout the program;
- Ensuring partners compliance with the donor and PIN guidelines, assisting with developing necessary operational manuals and SOPs for partners.

### **External and Internal Compliance**

- ensures the current contract templates used in the supervised departments on the country programme are up to date and properly used;
- conducts regular checks on proper archiving of accounting, procurement and logistics documents and sets up archiving rules if needed;
- coordinates external audits carried out at country programme level and assists with the HQ-level audits;
- is familiar with donors’ conditions and requirements and makes sure they are respected;
- acts as a communication channel between donors in case of any requests related to the finance, compliance and procurement agenda.

