Background

Kenya is scheduled to hold its next General Elections in 2027. Electoral cycles in Kenya have historically been associated with heightened political tension and, in some cases, violence, and the period ahead of 2027 is widely regarded by Government, development partners and the UN as a critical window for prevention. Kenya's National Cohesion and Integration Commission (NCIC) has developed a roadmap for a peaceful and violence-free 2027 electoral cycle, and national peace infrastructure mechanisms, including the National Steering Committee on Peacebuilding and Conflict Management (NSC) and the Uwiano Platform for Peace, play a central role in early warning and response.

The 2018 repositioning of the UN development system placed an empowered, independent and impartial Resident Coordinator at the centre of UN country-level coordination, supported by the Resident Coordinator's Office (RCO). Within the RCO, the Peace and Development Unit (PDU) supports the Resident Coordinator and UN Country Team on conflict prevention, peacebuilding, governance and electoral risk analysis, and on the design of an integrated, One UN approach to supporting peaceful, inclusive and credible elections.

Against this background, timely and rigorous political-economic analysis, systematic monitoring of online spaces for election-related risk, well-designed and well-monitored peacebuilding and election programming, and effective support to the Resident Coordinator's preventive diplomacy efforts are central to the UN's ability to support a peaceful electoral process in Kenya.

Purpose

The RCO Kenya Peace and Development Unit seeks a Political and Digital Risk Analyst to strengthen the UN's political-economic and digital risk-analysis capacity, support the design and monitoring of election and peacebuilding programming, and support the Resident Coordinator's preventive diplomacy efforts ahead of Kenya's 2027 General Elections. Housed in the PDU and working under the leadership of the Resident Coordinator, the staff member will support a coherent, evidence-based and preventive UN offer on peace, governance and elections.

Duties and Responsibilities

Under the overall guidance of the Resident Coordinator and the direct supervision of the Peace and Development Advisor, the staff member will support the Peace and Development Unit's contribution to a coherent, evidence-based and preventive UN approach to peace, governance and electoral risk in Kenya, with a particular focus on Kenya's preparations for the 2027 General Elections. This position will provide substantive analytical, monitoring, programmatic and diplomatic support across four inter-related areas of work.

Conduct political-economic analysis (PEA) to inform UN strategic positioning and programming

- Conduct regular political and political-economic analysis of national and county-level dynamics, including party politics, coalition dynamics, devolution, governance reforms, and their implications for peace, stability and development outcomes;

- Track and analyse political developments related to the 2027 electoral cycle, including the electoral calendar, legal and institutional reforms, the Independent Electoral and Boundaries Commission (IEBC), and county-level political and administrative dynamics;

- Analyse the political economy of key fiscal, resource-allocation and governance issues, including how budget processes, public resource management and corruption dynamics interact with political and electoral risk;

- Prepare concise, decision-ready political-economic analysis briefs, notes and updates for the Resident Coordinator, the Peace and Development Advisor and relevant UN inter-agency mechanisms;

- Contribute political-economic analysis inputs to the UN Country Analysis (UNCA), the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (UNSDCF) and other joint UN risk and context analysis products;

- Support the development and maintenance of structured political and conflict risk-analysis frameworks and tools, including tracking of structural drivers, triggers and early-warning indicators relevant to the electoral cycle;

- Liaise with think tanks, research institutions, academia, pollsters and analysts to access, validate and triangulate political-economic data and analysis;

- Contribute to an institutional knowledge base of political-economic analysis products for use across the RCO, PDU and UN Country Team (UNCT);

- Regular, decision-ready political-economic analysis briefs, notes and updates for the Resident Coordinator, the Peace and Development Advisor and UN inter-agency mechanisms. They will cover national and county dynamics, the 2027 electoral cycle and the political economy of fiscal and governance issues;

- A structured political and conflict risk-analysis framework that tracks structural drivers, triggers and early-warning indicators for the electoral cycle. Its findings will feed into the UNCA, the UNSDCF and other joint UN analysis products, and will be kept in a shared knowledge base, together with lessons learned and good practices.

Monitor social media and digital spaces for election-related risk identification

- Design and operate systematic monitoring of social media and digital platforms to identify hate speech, disinformation, incitement to violence and other indicators of election-related risk;

- Track online narratives, trends and virality relevant to electoral and social cohesion risks, including through the use of digital analytics, social listening tools and dashboards;

- Prepare regular social media and digital risk-monitoring reports and dashboards, flagging emerging patterns and risks for the Resident Coordinator, the Peace and Development Advisor and relevant UN and national counterparts, including the National Cohesion and Integration Commission (NCIC);

- Cross-reference online risk indicators with offline political, conflict and electoral data to strengthen the UN's overall early-warning picture;

- Support liaison with social media platforms, civil society fact-checking and digital-rights initiatives, and academic or technology partners on disinformation, hate speech and online mobilization trends;

- Contribute digital risk analysis and reporting to broader national and UN early-warning and prevention mechanisms, including the UWIANO Platform for Peace and the National Steering Committee on Peacebuilding and Conflict Management (NSC);

- Ensure that all social media and digital monitoring is conducted in line with data protection, privacy, do-no-harm and conflict-sensitivity principles;

- A functioning social media and digital monitoring system that produces regular reports and dashboards on hate speech, disinformation, incitement and online narratives. It will operate in line with data protection, privacy, do-no-harm and conflict-sensitivity principles;

- Integrated early-warning analysis that combines online and offline risk indicators. It will be shared with national and UN early-warning and prevention mechanisms, including the NCIC, the Uwiano Platform for Peace and the NSC.

Support the design, implementation and monitoring of election and peacebuilding programming

- Support the Peace and Development Unit and RCO in the design, implementation and monitoring of UN-supported election and peacebuilding programmes and projects, including successor initiatives to SECURE-Elections;

- Support results-based monitoring, data collection and reporting for election and peace-building projects and joint programmes, including those financed through the MPTF, Peacebuilding Fund (PBF) and other instruments;

- Support the development of concept notes, project documents, and progress and donor reports for peacebuilding and election-related programming;

- Liaise with implementing partners, including UN agencies, funds and programmes, non-governmental organisations and government counterparts, to track implementation progress and flag bottlenecks;

- Support the organisation of stakeholder consultations, technical working group meetings and validation workshops related to peacebuilding and election programming;

- Support monitoring of, and UN engagement with, the National Cohesion and Integration Commission (NCIC) roadmap and other national peace infrastructure and architecture initiatives;

- Results-based monitoring and progress reporting for UN-supported election and peace-building programmes and joint programmes, including those financed through the MPTF and the PBF.

Support the UN's preventive diplomacy efforts ahead of the 2027 elections

- Support the Resident Coordinator and Peace and Development Advisor in preparing briefing notes, talking points and scenario notes for engagement with government counterparts, political actors and diplomatic missions on prevention and electoral risk mitigation;

- Support coordination and secretariat functions for relevant good-offices and preventive diplomacy initiatives led by the Resident Coordinator;

- Support liaison with the diplomatic community, regional and international organizations (including the African Union, IGAD and the East African Community) and electoral observation missions, on shared risk analysis and coordinated messaging;

- Contribute to scenario-planning and contingency-planning exercises related to election-related tensions or violence, in support of UN preparedness;

- Support the documentation of good-offices and mediation-related engagements, ensuring appropriate confidentiality and discretion given the sensitivity of the subject matter;

- Support UN engagement with the National Steering Committee on Peacebuilding and Conflict Management (NSC), the Uwiano Platform for Peace, and other national peace infrastructure mechanisms;

- Draft key messages and talking points for the Resident Coordinator's engagements with the Executive, Parliament, the Independent Electoral and Boundaries Commission (IEBC) and county-level leadership on electoral prevention;

- Timely briefing notes, talking points, key messages and scenario notes for the Resident Coordinator’s engagements with the Executive, Parliament, the IEBC, county leadership, political actors and diplomatic missions. It also covers contributions to scenario-planning and contingency-planning exercises;

- Effective secretariat and liaison support for the Resident Coordinator’s good-offices and preventive diplomacy initiatives, with engagements documented confidentially. This covers national peace infrastructure (the NSC, the Uwiano Platform for Peace and the NCIC roadmap), the diplomatic community, the AU, IGAD, the EAC and electoral observation missions.

The incumbent performs other duties within their functional profile as deemed necessary for the efficient functioning of the Office and the Organization.

