Background

South Sudan continues to face significant peacebuilding challenges arising from political instability, intercommunal violence, economic hardship, displacement and recurrent climate-related shocks. Although the 2018 Revitalized Agreement on the Resolution of the Conflict in South Sudan (R-ARCSS) established a framework for peace and political transition, its implementation remains uneven. Renewed political tensions and insecurity, alongside delays in implementing key transitional benchmarks, have heightened uncertainty ahead of the elections scheduled for December 2026. These challenges underscore the importance of sustained investment in inclusive peacebuilding, conflict prevention and social cohesion.

In May 2021, South Sudan's eligibility to the UN Secretary-General's Peacebuilding Fund (PBF) was renewed for five years. PBF support is guided by a Strategic Results Framework focused on three priorities: (i) national democratization, justice and accountability; (ii) addressing displacement-related conflict; and (iii) strengthening local conflict prevention and peacebuilding. The PBF portfolio comprises 10 projects valued at approximately US$28.5 million, supporting nationally led peacebuilding efforts in collaboration with government institutions, UN entities and civil society partners.

The PBF Secretariat, situated within the UN Resident Coordinator's Office, provides strategic, technical and coordination support for the Fund's implementation in South Sudan. It facilitates engagement with the Ministry of Peacebuilding and other national stakeholders, supports the PBF Joint Steering Committee, and works with recipient UN organizations to strengthen program coherence, partnerships, monitoring, reporting and results-based management. The Secretariat also promotes alignment with the United Nations Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (2025–2029) and national development priorities.

The Secretariat comprises a Coordination Specialist, Finance and Administrative Associate, Monitoring and Evaluation Analyst, Program Management and Analysis Officer, and Driver. Against the backdrop of South Sudan's fragile political transition and evolving peacebuilding needs, the Secretariat plays a critical role in ensuring that PBF investments remain strategic, conflict-sensitive, responsive and focused on sustainable peacebuilding results.

Position Purpose

The PBF Secretariat M&E and Communications Analyst will support the development, implementation and maintenance of an integrated monitoring, evaluation and reporting system for the Peacebuilding Fund (PBF) portfolio in South Sudan, Aligned with the PBF Strategic Results Framework (SRF), the system will facilitate harmonized results tracking, promote synergies across projects and strengthen the measurement and reporting of collective peacebuilding outcomes against agreed portfolio priorities. The PBF Secretariat M&E and Communications Analyst will support the systematic collection, verification, consolidation and analysis of quantitative and qualitative data to monitor progress against SRF indicators, identify evidence gaps and strengthen results-based reporting.

Working closely with recipient agencies and implementing partners, the PBF Secretariat M&E and Communications Analyst will maintain updated results-tracking tools, project databases and geographic mapping of interventions; support field monitoring, perception surveys and other data collection activities; and facilitate the documentation of achievements, challenges and lessons learned.

The PBF Secretariat M&E and Communications Analyst will also support the operationalization and institutionalization of the PBF Community-Based Monitoring Mechanism, ensuring that community perspectives and feedback contribute to portfolio monitoring, accountability, program learning and adaptive management. In addition, the PBF Secretariat M&E and Communications Analyst will support strategic communications, visibility and knowledge management activities, translating monitoring findings and evidence of results into accessible communications and knowledge products. The Analyst will provide technical and operational support to the PBF portfolio evaluation and the preparation of South Sudan's request for renewed eligibility to the Fund.

Under the direct supervision of the PBF Coordination Specialist, the PBF Secretariat M&E and Communications Analyst will work closely with the RCO Monitoring and Evaluation Officer, RCO Communications Officer, other PBF Secretariat colleagues, recipient agencies and their implementing partners to strengthen the quality, coherence and effectiveness of portfolio monitoring, reporting, learning and communications.

Scope of Work

Under the overall supervision of the Head of RCO, reporting directly to the PBF Coordination Specialist and indirectly to PBSO, the M&E and Communications Analyst of the PBF Secretariat will work in close collaboration with the PBF Secretariat team and RCO colleagues to provide technical and operational support to the monitoring, evaluation, results reporting, community-based monitoring, strategic communications and knowledge management functions of the Peacebuilding Fund (PBF) Secretariat in South Sudan.

Ensure Portfolio Monitoring, Evaluation and Results-Based Reporting:

- Support the development, operationalization and periodic review of an integrated PBF portfolio monitoring, evaluation and reporting framework, aligned with the PBF Strategic Results Framework, including harmonization of indicators, baselines, targets, data collection methodologies and reporting tools to facilitate consistent monitoring of project performance and collective peacebuilding outcomes;

- Establish, maintain and regularly update portfolio monitoring and information management systems, including project databases, results-tracking matrices, indicator dashboards, implementation monitoring schedules and geographic mapping of PBF interventions, to facilitate systematic tracking, analysis and reporting of portfolio performance;

- Monitor implementation progress and results across PBF-funded projects, including through regular engagement with recipient agencies and implementing partners, review of project workplans and progress reports, verification of reported achievements and identification of implementation challenges, emerging risks and opportunities for program improvement;

- Plan, coordinate and participate in field monitoring missions, in collaboration with relevant Secretariat colleagues and project teams, to assess implementation progress, verify reported results, engage with beneficiaries and local stakeholders, and document findings, lessons learned and actionable recommendations;

- Support the preparation and quality assurance of PBF project and portfolio reports, including reviewing project progress reports, validating results information, consolidating portfolio achievements and contributing to PBF Secretariat reports and the PBF Joint Steering Committee annual report;

- Provide technical guidance and practical capacity-strengthening support to PBF recipient agencies and implementing partners on results-based management, indicator tracking, data collection, monitoring methodologies, reporting requirements and documentation of peacebuilding results.

Community-Based Monitoring, Participation and Accountability:

- Serve as the PBF Secretariat's operational focal point for the development, piloting, operationalization and progressive institutionalization of a standardized Community-Based Monitoring (CBM) Mechanism across the PBF portfolio, ensuring alignment with PBF guidance, the PBF Strategic Results Framework and relevant UN community engagement principles;

- Support the coordination and technical oversight of the CBM consultancy, including facilitating engagement with recipient agencies, implementing partners, government institutions, local authorities, civil society organizations and community representatives; monitoring progress against agreed workplans; and reviewing consultancy deliverables to ensure quality, relevance and practical applicability;

- Contribute to the development, review and validation of CBM methodologies, monitoring tools and operational systems, including community feedback instruments, perception monitoring indicators, digital data collection platforms, reporting templates, standard operating procedures and quality assurance protocols, ensuring complementarity with existing portfolio monitoring arrangements;

- Support the establishment, capacity strengthening and effective functioning of representative Community Monitoring Groups (CMGs) in selected PBF-supported locations, promoting meaningful participation of women, youth, persons with disabilities, traditional and faith-based leaders, and other community stakeholders;

- Coordinate and participate in the piloting and field implementation of the CBM mechanism, including supporting community monitoring activities, providing practical guidance to community monitors, verifying data quality, documenting implementation challenges and contributing to the refinement of monitoring tools and operational procedures;

- Facilitate the systematic collection, analysis and utilization of community-generated evidence, including beneficiary perceptions, feedback on project relevance and effectiveness, changes in local conflict dynamics, emerging risks and unintended consequences, and ensure that findings inform program adaptation, reporting, learning and strategic decision-making;

- Support the sustainability and progressive scale-up of the CBM mechanism, including maintaining relevant monitoring tools and databases, facilitating ongoing technical support to Community Monitoring Groups, tracking responses to community feedback and promoting adherence to ethical standards, safeguarding, confidentiality, data protection, conflict sensitivity and do-no-harm principles.

Strategic Communications, Visibility and Knowledge Sharing:

- Support the development, implementation and periodic review of a portfolio-wide PBF strategic communications and visibility strategy, in close collaboration with the RCO Communications Officer, recipient agencies and implementing partners, to strengthen awareness and understanding of PBF priorities, achievements and contributions to peacebuilding in South Sudan;

- Develop and maintain an annual PBF communications and visibility workplan, identifying priority activities, target audiences, key messages, communications products, dissemination channels, timelines and responsibilities, and monitor progress against agreed deliverables;

- Develop and disseminate high-quality strategic communications and visibility products, including human-interest and impact stories, results briefs, factsheets, newsletters, infographics, presentations, web articles, social media content, photographs and audiovisual materials that communicate PBF achievements, lessons learned and contributions to peacebuilding outcomes;

- Coordinate communications and visibility activities across PBF-funded projects, including providing technical guidance to recipient agencies and implementing partners on strategic messaging, branding, visibility requirements and documentation of results, while ensuring coherence with relevant PBF and UN communications guidelines;

- Identify, document and communicate compelling evidence of peacebuilding results and impact, drawing on project monitoring, community-based monitoring, evaluations and beneficiary perspectives, and ensuring that communications products are accurate, inclusive, conflict-sensitive and developed with appropriate consent;

- Establish and maintain a systematic portfolio-wide knowledge management system, including organized repositories of project documentation, monitoring reports, community-generate evidence, evaluation findings, communication products, good practices and lessons learned, to support institutional memory and evidence-informed decision-making;

- Support knowledge sharing, learning and strategic outreach, including preparing thematic briefs, case studies and results summaries; organizing learning events and technical exchanges; and providing communications and visibility support to high-level meetings, field missions, contributing partner visits and PBF Joint Steering Committee activities.

Portfolio Evaluation, Re-eligibility and Program Coordination Support:

- Provide substantive technical and coordination support to the planning and implementation of the PBF portfolio evaluation, including compiling and organizing project documentation, monitoring data, community-generated evidence, results reports and other relevant information; facilitating stakeholder consultations and field missions; and contributing to the review of evaluation deliverables;

- Support the coordination of the portfolio evaluation consultancy, including facilitating engagement with recipient agencies, implementing partners and relevant stakeholders, tracking agreed workplans and deliverables, supporting validation and learning processes, and monitoring follow-up on evaluation recommendations;

- Contribute to the preparation of South Sudan's request for renewed eligibility to the PBF, including compiling and synthesizing portfolio results, evaluation findings, community monitoring evidence, lessons learned and relevant background information to demonstrate achievements, continuing peacebuilding needs and emerging programming priorities;

- Support research, consultations and documentation processes associated with the re-eligibility application, including coordinating inputs from recipient agencies, implementing partners and other stakeholders, and preparing results summaries, analytical briefs, presentations, and supporting annexes and other substantive documentation;

- Support coordination between the PBF Secretariat, recipient agencies and implementing partners on monitoring, evaluation, community-based monitoring, reporting and communications requirements, including facilitating information sharing, tracking agreed actions and following up on relevant deliverables;

- Provide technical and organizational support to PBF project Technical Working Groups, portfolio coordination meetings and PBF Joint Steering Committee meetings, including preparing portfolio performance updates, results summaries, evaluation and community monitoring findings, briefing materials and meeting documentation, and tracking agreed follow-up actions;

- Contribute monitoring, evaluation and communications inputs to portfolio planning, partner engagement and resource mobilization processes, including through preparation of evidence-based briefing materials, strategic messaging and documentation of PBF achievements and catalytic contributions to peacebuilding in South Sudan.

